# PowerCycleTest_PythonBeta - parameter reference

Source: `C:\apex_junczhai@amd.com\testflows\public\execute_power_cycle_test_python.html`

`kind` legend: **enum** fixed value domain / **text** free text or number / **server-populated** filled by the APEX server, resolve at build time / **runtime-injected** written by APEX itself, never generate it / **hidden-const** not shown in the dialog.

`origin` legend: blank keeps the APEX flow default / **PMM** a constant this team always overrides / **SLOT** resolved per run, see the checklist below / APEX injected by APEX itself.

## Slots to resolve (2)

These are **not** in the template. A required slot is omitted rather than filled with a placeholder, and the build refuses to emit JSON until it is supplied. If the route below cannot be resolved for the station under test, raise a clarification - do not carry the Example value over.

### `Options.powertest` (required)

- **Route**: From the scenario the ATM case names, via the mode table in the apex-powercycletest skill: S0i3 / Modern Standby -> 'Modern Standby: Entry-OS Standby, Event-, Exit-HPET Wake'; Restart -> 'Restart: Entry-OS Restart, Event-, Exit-'; S4 / Hibernate -> 'S4: Entry-OS Hibernate, Event-, Exit-HPET Wake'; S5 / Shutdown -> 'S5: Entry-OS Shutdown, Event-, Exit-Relay Power On'. The full enum has 38 values including Linux: and Chrome: variants and AIM-T, S3, G3 and combined Modern Standby-S4-OS forms; take the exact string from the field domain, never retype it.
- **Example**: `Modern Standby: Entry-OS Standby, Event-, Exit-HPET Wake` (S0i3, woken by HPET rather than a relay) - captured on 2026-09-11. Illustrative, not authoritative.
- **Scope of that example**: the most common PMM scenario; the other three reference items use the Restart, S4 and S5 rows of the same table
- **If unresolved**: clarify with the case owner - do not default to the flow's own default (S5), which is not the scenario PMM runs most

### `Options.loops` (required)

- **Route**: The loop count the ATM case asks for. Flow default is 1. Measured across 16 real items in two queues: 1 (10 items), 3 (2 items) and 10 (4 items). It does not appear in this queue's varying set only because all four items of 04-Juncai-PMM_Feature.Quick.Check happen to run 10.
- **Example**: `10` (ten entry/resume cycles) - captured on 2026-09-11. Illustrative, not authoritative.
- **Scope of that example**: the 04-Juncai-PMM_Feature.Quick.Check value, not a standard - the case decides; 08-Juncai-PMM_Infrastructure uses 1 and 3
- **If unresolved**: clarify - a wrong loop count silently produces a shorter or longer test that still reports Pass

