## Open questions

- A passing run does not leave a sleepstudy HTML behind, even with Sleep Study.sleepstudyhtml = yes, which is the entire reason the HelperScripts module exists. Whether that is an APEX defect or intended behaviour is UNVERIFIED - it is recorded here as observed behaviour of 5.5.0.6, not as a diagnosis.
- The Restart reference item carries --loops=10 but --helperonstopscriptargs='-logname sleepstudy-report_Reboot', with no -loops at all. This is NOT a loop-count defect: a Restart run does not need the sleepstudy report, so nothing reads the helper's output. The item is over-configured rather than mis-configured - the clean form for Restart is to detach the whole HelperScripts module, not to add the missing -loops.
- Ten items of 08-Juncai-PMM_Infrastructure have the helper attached, --loops=1, and no -loops. They are plausibly correct via the helper script's own default, but that default is UNVERIFIED - it is not in the queue and has to be read out of the helper script once. Until then those ten are WARN, not clean.
- --pctworkload=none in all four items, so the entire Workload block below it never executes. operatingsystemtype=Windows, workload=314be6b7-aaf4-eb11-b563-281878b51121, workloadpreset and workloadrunparameters all differ from the form default but are INERT - they are copy-paste inheritance, not PMM policy, and are deliberately not listed as fixed. Do not promote them.

